      "name": "--ds-fg-disabled",
      "type": "color",
      "role": "Disabled text without opacity. WCAG 2.2 SC 1.4.3 exempts text in inactive user interface components; holding this entry to the 4.5:1 text threshold is what previously forced fg-muted, fg-meta and fg-disabled onto one value and made unavailable controls indistinguishable from ordinary metadata. It must stay visibly weaker than --ds-fg-meta, and why a control is disabled must be stated in readable text nearby (design-system.md 7.1), never implied by this color alone.",
